/-!
# The common-core odd-degree argument

The actual cubic subgroup in D₀ has no fixed points on P or V. Its scalar
image in SL₃ contradicts coprime action on P, proving odd field degree.
This identifies the full Hall group with D₀, puts the original Sylow in L,
and supplies the literal elementary quotient T/P of order q². These
conclusions require only the earlier source state in OrthogonalInput.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, printed p.774.
-/
